From 95f70512784cb381d55f14ac5f1acac801534617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] tests/vizzbox_golden.c: the songs of the Vizzbox 1.0,
 bit for bit (the 1.1 golden)

With nobody's hand on the controls the Vizzbox 1.1 must make the songs 1.0 made (BRIEF-VIZZBOX-1.1.md 1, 9):
every subgenre of 1.0 with three seeds (each with its own ENERGY and VARIATION) in every LENGTH (SHORT and
NORMAL to their end, ENDLESS 180 s) and ENDLESS ten minutes twice, 326 songs: everything the unit sends over
USB MIDI (each byte, the clock too, with the sample it went out by) and its audio, each as a hash.
tests/vizzbox_golden10.txt was made by this file built against Vizzbox 1.0's tree (patches 0001-0014);
tests/run_tests.sh compares.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawochSWXFaES57pjc4r
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
